This is a copy of curses, the cursor motion and screen optimization package,as released with Berkeley 4.3BSD Unix.  It was written by Ken Arnold whileat Berkeley, and is:/* * Copyright 1980 Kenneth C. R. C. Arnold and The Regents of the * University of California.  Permission is granted to freely * distribute curses and its documentation provided that this * notice is left intact. */There is no Unix source code in it.  However, to accomplish this, theguts of the routines printw() and scanw() have been removed and replaced.John Gilmore changed printw() to call vsprintf().  I would have changedscanw() too, but apparently there is no vsscanf()!One bug fix has been applied, in cr_tty.c, to avoid stomping theenvironment variables when longname() sets the terminal type.	-- John Gilmore[Contributed July 29, 1987 to the Sun User Group tape by: 	Kenneth C. R. C. Arnold	apollo!arnoldThe ownership of the code is explained above.]